extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 36: Sovietski printed 95-98 (cache p095-p098, cache page = printed folio + 0 for printed 38-177), a text layer with clean figures on these pages. Heading Cyborg Soldier O.C.C. (printed 95); the stat block is Sovietski Cyborg Soldier O.C.C. Stats (printed 97) and ends on printed 98 above Police Officer O.C.C. A military full conversion cyborg soldier, so occ_group men-of-arms and men_of_arms true. || XP: the Experience Tables (printed 224, cache p220) print three Cyborg Soldier ladders, by body: Light Machine, Heavy Machine and Superheavy Machine. A variant cannot override xp_table, so the Light Machine ladder is stored and the other two are in GM Notes. || BONUSES: +1 M.E., +1 strike, parry and dodge, +1 pull punch, +1 roll with impact and +3 save vs Horror Factor stored. The full conversion penalties are prose. || HIT POINTS AND S.D.C.: none printed; a full conversion cyborg''s M.D.C. lives in its body, which is a vessel row (rows 30-39 of the Sovietski plan: ~394 to ~398, and the WB17 Thunderhammer, Thunderstrike and Thunderstorm), named in restrictions. || SKILLS: the Pilot pick is the printed five, Hovercraft (Ground) being the catalog''s Hover Craft (ground). Literacy: Russian is printed as the native language at +10% and stored at catalog base plus 10; Language: Russian is printed at +20%, not as a native figure, and stored so. Hand to Hand: Expert prints no upgrade price, so no hand_to_hand block. || M.O.S.: the three Cyborg Corps packages are skills.mos options; their M.O.S. Bonuses are a parallel pick-one Training group. Skill-percentage bonuses there (+5% or +10% to Climbing, Swimming, Radio: Basic) and conditional Perception are prose. The SPK upgrade to Martial Arts is a granted Hand to Hand: Martial Arts, which replaces Expert. Lore: D-Bees is the catalog''s Lore: D-Bee. The Pilot exclusions for Power Armor, Robots, Fighter Jets, Ships and Tanks & APCs are spelled as the catalog rows for those, with the robot and power armor combat rows and Fighter Combat. The nine Infantry Soldier packages the book also offers are described on printed 101 on, outside this class''s pages, and are not options; the mos note names them. || SECONDARY: one each at levels 2, 5, 8 and 13, none at level 1. || MONEY: a salary only, so no starting_money. || EQUIPMENT: the AK energy rifle is a pick of the three Sovietski laser Kalashnikovs (row 2 weapons); the I.D., the body''s own kit, the pistol and the weapon per W.P. are restrictions prose."
