## Lore

The Sovietski has fielded Light and Heavy Machines for generations, and its
newer Superheavy Machines are its answer to the strange cyborgs of the
Warlords. Lacking robot and power armor programs of its own, the nation poured
its effort into bionics: Light and Heavy Machines fill the role power armor
plays elsewhere, and the Superheavies stand in for full-sized combat robots,
teething troubles and all. Its cyborg troops are reckoned the best trained in
Russia, matched only by those of the NGR and the Coalition.

Every Cyborg Soldier serves in one of three corps of the Red Army. The SPK
(Svete Priznaniya Kiborga) is light infantry and reconnaissance: mostly Light
Machines that scout behind enemy lines, track raiders and Brodkil to their
dens, sabotage supply lines and hunt enemy cyborgs for salvage. The MPO
(Mobil''noye Podrazdeleniye Oberony) is the fast-response force of Light and
Heavy Machines, flown or driven to a Rift, a raid or an incursion to hold the
line until more troops arrive. The BDK (Bronirovannyy Desantnyy Korpus) is
armored assault, Heavy and Superheavy Machines that act as a tank corps
without the tanks.

Candidates are screened and conditioned hard for life as a metal warrior
before conversion.

## GM Notes

Experience by body (printed 224): the Light Machine ladder is the one stored.
Heavy Machine: 2,151 / 4,301 / 8,601 / 18,601 / 26,601 / 36,601 / 54,601 /
75,601 / 99,601 / 135,601 / 185,601 / 240,601 / 290,601 / 343,601 for levels 2
to 15. Superheavy Machine: 2,501 / 5,001 / 10,001 / 20,001 / 30,001 / 40,001 /
55,001 / 80,001 / 105,001 / 150,001 / 200,001 / 250,001 / 310,001 / 380,001.

Instead of a corps package the soldier may take one of the nine Infantry
Soldier M.O.S. packages (see the Sovietski Infantry Soldier); grant its skills
by hand.

On assignment: any military transport on a Sovietski support mission, extra
weapons including Heavy and Superheavy Machine handheld weapons, E-Clips,
vehicles, medical kits, cameras, surveillance gear and explosives (fusion
blocks included); medium-level clearance, and priority for S.C.U.B.A. gear,
heavy weapons, explosives and cybernetic repairs. Availability depends on the
commander, stock, location, casualties and combat conditions.

Cybernetics and bionics come with the body; more can be bought, awarded for
heroism or issued for a mission. Superheavy cyborgs are usually given a
Proletarian Light Machine or similar human-sized body for private life, and
every soldier gets a light frame on retiring from the army.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sovietski-cyborg-soldier');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sovietski-cyborg-soldier';

